course: dictionary
lesson: 1002
title: Boldly: brave, clear, or cheeky
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words tell you how someone does something. Boldly is one of them. It tells you the way an action happens. «She stepped boldly into the cave» means she walked in without being afraid. Ask yourself: how did she step? The answer is boldly.
explain: Boldly can also describe how something looks. «Boldly coloured» means the colours are bright and strong, so they are easy to see. Here boldly has nothing to do with courage. It means clear and strong.
explain: The words around boldly give clues. In «Toad walked boldly up to the sentries at Toad Hall», he is in disguise and still goes straight up to them. That takes courage. Sometimes boldly can also mean a bit too confident, so look at the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Boldly is an adverb, so it tells you how an action is done.
fact: «Boldly» means in a brave, confident way, not afraid of danger.
fact: «Boldly» can also mean in a way that is easy to see, strong and clear, as in «boldly coloured».
fact: «Boldly» can sometimes mean in a cheeky, too confident way.
fact: The Star Trek line «to boldly go where no one has gone before» uses boldly to show that the explorers go bravely.
exercise: «She stepped boldly into the cave.» What does boldly mean here? | In a quiet, sleepy way | In a slow, tired way | *In a brave, confident way | In a wet, muddy way
exercise: «The painting was boldly coloured, with red and gold everywhere.» What does boldly mean here? | *Bright and strong, easy to see | Very old and faded | Sad and grey | Brave and fearless
exercise: Find and copy one word that is an adverb showing how someone acts. «He spoke boldly to the teacher.» | to | spoke | teacher | *boldly
test: «Toad walked boldly up to the sentries at Toad Hall.» What does boldly show about Toad? | He was hungry for breakfast | He was tired and slow | *He was brave and daring | He was lost and afraid
test: Jayden says, «Boldly means the same as loudly.» Is he right? | Yes, boldly always means loudly | Yes, boldly means quietly | No, boldly means only in the morning | *No, boldly means brave, clear or cheeky, not loud
exam: «Ella boldly raised her hand to answer the hard question.» Which meaning fits best, and why? | Faded and old, because the paint had dried | Wet and grey, because it was raining | Tired and sleepy, because she yawned first | *Brave and confident, because she was not afraid to speak up
